## What S3 already has
- **Prelude** (`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc`):
  - `py/yield-from` (line 587) forwards sends and throws to the inner generator, closes the inner first, and turns `StopIteration` into a return value.
  - The `:iterator` cell (`{:py/type :iterator :src :i}`) is used in `py/iterable` and `py/iter-at` (line 2219, index signature kept per ruling 5), plus `py/next`, the `iter`/`next` builtins and the `__next__`/`__iter__` methods.
- **Lowering:** `lower-yield` in `lower.cljc:1777` turns `yield from x` into `(py/yield-from %gen x)`.
- **JVM tests on all four evaluators**, in `test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:543-890`:
  - Every row of the S3 acceptance table: send-through (`1, got s, v r, 10, 20`), a throw reaching the inner's handler, close order (inner before outer), `yield from range(3000)` (a `^:slow` test), and `iter([1,2])` giving `1 2 d` and `True`.
  - Extra cases: a `StopIteration` thrown through a closed delegate, a three-deep chain resumed from different callers, and suspension while an exception unwinds.
  - The JVM-only check that reachable heap stays the same under nested delegation (`reachable-heap-is-stable-under-delegation-test`, `^:slow`), per ruling 7.
- **Node/Dart parity tests** in `prelude_parity_test.cljc`: `yield-from-and-iter-on-every-host-test`, `delegation-stop-and-sticky-dict-iterator-on-every-host-test` and `delegation-chain-callers-and-unwinding-on-every-host-test`.

